load @term/seed/theory/category
  find category

# A functor: a structure-preserving map between categories, sending objects to objects and morphisms to morphisms so
# that identities and composition are preserved. Functors are the morphisms of the category of categories, and they are
# how one kind of mathematics is translated into another (the fundamental group is a functor from spaces to groups). The
# form carries the source and target categories; the identity-and-composition-preserving laws are the conditions.
form functor
  link source, like category
  link target, like category
